# index.html contracts

One HtmlService page. Tailwind CDN, Inter, Dew 2.0 type scale (12 / 14 / 18 / 24, weights 400–600), Dew surfaces and brand blue `#276cf0`. `en-IN` currency. No build step. Heat-map fills come from `getHeatmapStyle`. Cells have no border. Corpus and Net Profit use the absolute-return color. NAV, units, and invested stay plain. Percents use `formatPct` (`12.3%`, one decimal, no plus on gains). Table amounts are whole rupees. Every table uses the shared `.sheet` rules: IBM Plex Sans at weight 500 with tabular lining figures, `heatChip` for heat-map cells, `fundNameCell` for the frozen Fund Name, and the same header helpers. Labels stay Inter. Do not use a monospace face or a second figure face for amounts or rates.

## Chrome
- View dropdown in the header, immediately before **Refresh Data**: `matrix` (Return Matrix), `compare` (Fund Comparator), `risk` (Risk and Rating), `overlap` (Portfolio Overlap), or `final` (Summary). Summary gives one keep, switch, or start note per category, with pros and cons. A fund counts as held only when it is marked held. Switch is named only when the 3-year or 5-year CAGR lead is at least 2 points, max drawdown is not worse by more than 3 points, and the illustrated next year at the past 3-year pace is still ahead after tax and exit load. Switch pros name Sharpe, Sortino, and drawdown. Switch cons price equity LTCG at 12.5% after one ₹1.25 lakh exemption on that card, STCG at 20% on SIP lots under 12 months, and an assumed 1% exit load on those young lots. The sheet does not store the scheme's real exit load. Custom Range XIRR is context. Risk cells use the same heat colors. Green is the better end of that ratio, so lower-is-better figures are flipped before coloring. Within each category on the Risk table, the same category leader used by Summary gets the light fill, even when that fund was not checked. That leader prefers funds with a 3-year or 5-year record. A missing figure scores as the weak end, not as an average.
- Theme control fixed bottom left: Light / Dark / System, stored as `mf-matrix-theme`. `html.dark` swaps Dew tokens. Empty heat cells follow the active theme.
- Page must fit desktop and phone. `overflow-x: hidden` on the page. Below 768px, KPI cards are 2×2, the matrix scrolls inside `.matrix-scroll`, only Fund Name stays frozen, and the group header row is hidden.

## Return Matrix
`allFunds`, `currentDisplayFunds`, `top2FilterActive` (default true), `activeMetric` (`xirr` | `cagr`), sort default `1Y` descending.
Changing SIP amount, SIP day, or dates calls `getFundMatrixData` once for the whole book. A tab switch does not fetch again. Only the visible tab is drawn; the others draw when opened. Filters, Top 2, sort, and the metric switch stay in the browser.
- Category, AMC, and Scheme are checkbox lists with Select All. Select All applies no restriction. The three lists intersect. Top 2 then keeps two schemes per remaining category by the active 1Y series when the scheme selection is All.
- The matrix toolbar, immediately before Top 2 / Cat, has a fund search. It multi-selects schemes and includes All and None. It writes the same scheme selection as the Scheme filter, Fund Comparator, Risk and Rating, Portfolio Overlap, and Summary. All follows the matrix rows, so Top 2 (when on) is the shared list on every tab. Checking or unchecking a fund copies those rows into an explicit list used by every tab. None selects nothing.
- Fund checklists share `fundChecklistHtml`. The matrix search, Fund Comparator, Risk and Rating, and Portfolio Overlap group the book by category inside `.fund-picker`. Summary’s “Funds you hold” list uses that same checklist and scroller, limited to the shared shortlist, and checks `heldFunds`.
- SIP amount, SIP day, From Date, To Date, and Sale Date sit above the tabs and apply to every tab. There is no second copy of those inputs.
- Tenures, in order: `5D` `15D` `1M` `3M` `6M` `9M` `1Y` `2Y` `3Y` `5Y` `7Y` `10Y` `12Y`. Groups are Short and Long. Keep columns compact. SIP XIRR hides `5D` and `15D`. Trailing CAGR still shows them.
- The SIP XIRR / Trailing CAGR switch re-renders tenure cells only. Custom Range XIRR, SIP Corpus, Net Profit, and Absolute return do not follow it.
- Every metric column has a sort icon. Nulls sort last.
- Desktop freeze: `#` and Fund Name. There is no Code column. Drag the Fund Name header edge to set its width; the width is stored as `mf-matrix-name-width` and the column stays frozen. Move up is green, move down is red, 1px apart, and exempt from the 32px button height. Up/down reorders the current view only.

## Fund Comparator
The shared shortlist is the matrix rows while All is on, and the checked funds after a manual change. Unchecked, that shortlist is one pool, plus the overall leader. **Compare within category** adds the leader of each selected fund’s full category.
Max benefit is the highest `customRangeXirr` for the same SIP (From, To, amount, day). Net profit breaks a tie. Sale Date does not pick the winner. The table always shows the best of the selected funds and the overall leader across every tracked scheme. The comparator always starts with a **Your selection** table of the checked funds, including the overall leader when that fund was not checked. With **Compare within category** checked, every category then gets its own table under that, stacked one after another. Every comparator table is the full window width. Fund Name uses the same `--name-width` as the Return Matrix, and the same drag handle on the header edge changes that width for both tabs. The other columns share the remaining width. Each card shows the leader of that category’s full list. That leader’s invested amount, corpus, and net profit are multiplied by how many selected funds are in the category, as if every one of those SIPs went into that one fund. Rates stay unscaled.
Comparator, risk, and matrix amounts are whole rupees. Percentages keep one decimal and do not prefix a plus on gains. Those tables reuse the matrix money and rate cells.
Table columns stay compact: rank, fund, invested, corpus, net profit, absolute, custom XIRR, then `3M` `6M` `1Y` `3Y` `5Y` `10Y` from the active series. There is no category column. The category leader row has a light fill. Other winning marks stay on the rank cell.

## Portfolio Overlap
Uses the shared shortlist. **Load overlap** calls `getFundOverlap` for 2 to 10 funds. The matrix cell is pairwise equity overlap: the sum of the smaller weight of each stock held by both funds. Fund names wrap inside equal square cells. The diagonal is blank. Higher overlap is the red end. A scheme is omitted from the numbers when the published portfolio does not match its scheme code. Cash and debt are excluded. Switching tabs does not fetch again.
